iwlwifi: restore the lar_disable module parameter

LAR (Location Aware Regulatory) lets the firmware own the regulatory
domain: the wiphy is registered SELF_MANAGED and cfg80211 ignores every
user hint.  On an AX200 whose firmware table keeps the 5 GHz band
passive-scan only, no country ever reaches the phy, so hostapd cannot
start an AP above 2.4 GHz (nl80211 answers NO-IR / "Could not select
hw_mode and channel").  Upstream removed the escape hatch in
f06021a18fcf ("iwlwifi: remove lar_disable module parameter"), which
leaves no way to hand the decision back to the regdb.

Restore it: with iwlwifi.lar_disable=1 the driver takes the pre-LAR
path -- no self-managed flag, no MCC init -- and the in-kernel
regulatory database applies, as it did until 5.4.

